# SPA fallback for Cloudflare Pages and Netlify.
#
# The app routes on the client: /network and /board/<id> are real URLs to the
# router and nothing on disk. Without this rule the host 404s anything but /,
# so the site works until someone presses reload or opens a shared link -- the
# same trap the FastAPI mount needed a subclass to avoid.
#
# The /api rule comes first so the exported JSON is served as itself rather
# than being rewritten to the HTML shell, which fails as a confusing JSON
# parse error rather than as a 404.
/api/*  /api/:splat  200
/*      /index.html  200
